// Copy this file to Signing.xcconfig and fill in your own values:
//
//     cp ios/Config/Signing.xcconfig.example ios/Config/Signing.xcconfig
//
// Signing.xcconfig is gitignored on purpose. Signing identity is per-developer:
// a bundle identifier registered to one Apple Developer team cannot be signed
// by another. Committing these values breaks every other developer's build with
// "No profiles for '<bundle id>' were found".
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM
//   Your 10-character Apple Developer Team ID.
//   Xcode > Settings > Accounts > pick your team; the ID is in parentheses.
//
// PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER
//   Must be unique to YOU — reverse-DNS on a domain or name you control.
//   Never reuse a teammate's. Bundle ids are globally unique to one Apple
//   team, and the Meta Wearables app registration is keyed to the bundle id
//   too, so sharing one means whoever does not own it gets signing failures
//   and silent glasses-registration failures. One id per developer:
//     com.mocinjay.clipso     — Allen Williams
//     com.ajdinahmedi.clipso  — Ajdin Ahmedi
//   Add your own line rather than borrowing either of these.
//
// Free "Personal Team" accounts get 7-day provisioning profiles. When the app
// stops launching after a week, rebuild from Xcode and it reissues. They also
// cannot sign the Wi-Fi entitlements the glasses' high-bandwidth link needs, so
// on a Personal Team uncomment the CLIPSO_ENTITLEMENTS line below: the build
// then streams over Bluetooth only (about 504x896, frame rate as the link allows).

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345

// Set your id ONCE here. The app takes it as-is; the ClipsoWidgets extension
// derives its own id underneath it, because Apple requires an extension's
// bundle id to be prefixed by its containing app's. Never write the literal id
// anywhere else or the two drift and the extension fails to install.
CLIPSO_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.clipso
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = $(CLIPSO_BUNDLE_ID)

// Personal Team only — see above.
// CLIPSO_ENTITLEMENTS =

// MWDAT_CLIENT_TOKEN
//   The Client Token from Wearables Developer Center. Leave it empty while the
//   glasses run in Developer Mode (MetaAppID 0); set it, together with a real
//   MetaAppID, for any other release channel.
MWDAT_CLIENT_TOKEN =
